{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he took the knife.</b> He said: My father, do not tell my mother when she stands on the roof or when she stands at the mouth of the pit, lest she fall and die. When he wished to slaughter him, ויקרא אליו מלאך ה' מן השמים ויאמר אברהם אברהם — twice, because he was hurrying to slaughter him. ויאמר אל תשלח ידך. He said to Him: Who are you? He said to him: I am an angel. He said to Him: When it was said to me קח את בנך — He Himself said it to me; and now if He desires, let Him say it to me Himself. Immediately, ויקרא מלאך ה' שנית מן השמים. He said to him: בי נשבעתי נאם ה' וגו'. He said to Him: Master of all the world! You swore, and I swore that I would not step down from the altar until I say to You what I need. You did not tell me כה יהיה זרעך — from whom? He said to him: From Yitzhak. He said to Him: Master of all the world! Just as it was in my heart to answer You back — yesterday You said to me כי ביצחק יקרא לך זרע, and now You say to me והעלהו לעולה, yet I subdued my impulse and did not answer — so too, when my children sin and enter into trouble, may You remember for them this Akedah, and may it be counted before You as though their ashes were piled upon the altar and as though their blood were dashed before You on the altar, and may You pardon all their iniquities."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:10.873368356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}